# src/apps/daemon/internal/analysis/immunization

## Purpose
Autonomous Self-Immunization Engine: detects real-time DPI middlebox interference (RST injection, SNI reset, handshake dropout), dynamically tests evasion recipes, and maintains an in-memory and persistent Immune Memory of evasion antibodies.

## Contents
- `types.go`: Core data models: `InterferenceType`, `EvasionAntibody`, `PacketTimingProfile`.
- `detector.go`: Non-invasive passive detector diagnosing middlebox interference from connection failures and timing anomalies.
- `synthesizer.go`: Active ladder synthesizer testing evasion variations to discover winning antibodies.
- `store.go`: Thread-safe Immune Memory cache providing domain matching, efficacy scoring, and JSON export/import.

## Interfaces and dependencies
Imported by daemon runtime and routing layers to diagnose interference and select tested evasions. Belongs to the analysis layer and depends on lower-level protocol and foundation packages.

## Invariants
Interference observations and stored antibody semantics remain stable for callers; shared store access stays concurrency-safe; probe or synthesis failure must not be silently promoted into a successful antibody, and persisted state must be validated before use.